message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite the software release."
type: software
title: "False-Positive Persistence Toolkit"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Tongchen
version: "0.2.1"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23907914"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/tzhangaca/fp-persistence-toolkit"
url: "https://github.com/tzhangaca/fp-persistence-toolkit"
abstract: >-
  A Python toolkit for descriptive comparison of repeated false-positive
  recurrence across fitted fraud-screening model instances. It uses the
  fp-persistence-audit engine to audit a shared legitimate-transaction population
  and checks input compatibility and context-specific false-positive allocation.
keywords:
  - fraud screening
  - false-positive persistence
  - model auditing
  - machine learning evaluation
